 since his  awakening the more his new powers and  abilities are starting to manifest and  the more dangerous he becomes  as expected the heroes are all very  worried  about gran torino and they want to tend  to his wounds  as soon as possible but unfortunately  they have to take care of shigaraki  first  and that is no easy task and as deku and  ryukyu struggle to restrain shigaraki  deku realizes that shigaraki has a quirk  destroying bullet  deku recognizes right away what a  massive threat  this small object poses and he hits  shigaraki with a 100  wyoming smash the shock waves from the  impact  throw up dust and debris all over the  place and it is honestly pretty crazy to  see deku just using 100  so casually it makes sense because this  is a drastic situation  it doesn't get any more drastic than  this but i just have to point out that  deku  has definitely come a long way since the  beginning of the story  although to be fair so has shigaraki  also  shout out to wyoming that's not a state  you see mentioned very often  so if there is anyone watching this  video from wyoming  definitely drop me a line down in the  comments there's probably at least like  two of you out there  endeavor and bakugou then rush into the  aftermath of deku's smash  but as the dust clears we see that  shigaraki is still very much  conscious shigaraki had bitten down on  deku's forearm in order to keep deku  from blowing him away  and this came at the price of  shigaraki's lower teeth  all of shigaraki's lower teeth seemed to  have been smashed to bits  as a result of one for all's power  what's more  in the next few shots we see that  shigaraki did manage to launch  another bullet it appears that he had  more than one bullet stashed away  and this second bullet hits izawa right  in the left leg  just below the knee however the absolute  mad lad  isawa realized what was about to happen  and as the bullet hit him  he literally sliced off his own leg to  prevent the contents of the bullet from  spreading through his body  as he did this izawa thought of arie and  it was her  innocence and her smile that gave him  the strength to do what had to be done  in this crucial moment bruh this was  absolutely unreal we all knew that eizel  was a badass  but this move cutting off his own leg  without hesitation  was a whole other level of badassery  even shigaraki acknowledges how cool  aizawa is but shigaraki is also  determined to complete his mission  so he won't let his admiration for izawa  prevent him from doing what has to be  done  shigaraki is then able to break through  the hero lines and launch himself  forward  until he is literally touching aizawa's  face  deku manages to hold on to shigaraki  with a one-handed black whip  but shigeru is just too fast and strong  and deku cannot restrain him  on his own luckily just as shigaraki is  about to disintegrate isaac's face  into a million pieces a sudden barrage  of ice  tears into shigaraki and this pushes  shigaraki  away from izawa that's right our boy  shoto todoroki is finally on the scene  and he is ready to protect his teacher  at all cost  just like deku and bakugo deku uses this  opportunity to hit shigaraki with  another epic punch  and shigaraki is thrown further back and  away from  aizawa nevertheless izawa is clearly  injured and he has blood  running over his eyes deck when the  others are worried about izawa but he  isn't the only one that they should be  worrying about  due to the fact that isil had to close  his eyes shigaraki's quirks have  all been reactivated and as he stands up  after being hit by dekku we can see that  chicago's body has already recovered  from all of the massive damage that it  had sustained  just moments ago shigaraki proclaims  that despite their best efforts to  protect izawa  the only thing that awaits the heroes is  destruction shigaraki is confident that  victory is inevitable  and as the newly regenerated shigaraki  rises from the ashes  the chapter switches focus back to the  class 1a students who are working on  evacuating the civilians of jakku  as the students are wondering what  happened to todoroki since he had  apparently gone out to find  deku and bakugo an important piece of  news shocks the civilians  in the crowd ida asks one of the  civilians to turn up the broadcast  and the reporter announces that a  gigantic villain is on his way to jakku  this villain is destroying everything in  his path and it looks like he is going  to smash through  multiple cities before finally arriving  in jakku  uraka is surprised because she knows  that most of the pro heroes were  assigned  to keeping the villains from the mansion  at bay and  then the final page shows a transformed  gigantomachia about to smash  his way through a city and as this  happens oblivious civilians are going  about their day just meters away  blissfully unaware  that everything around them is about to  be destroyed  we can see that gigantomachia's body has  changed  not only did his jaw go up over his eyes  as we saw in previous chapters but his  hands  seem to have transformed as well it  appears that his hands have now expanded  in a way that makes them more suitable  for bursting through obstacles and  annihilating  everything in sight and unfortunately  we all know what this means this means  the plan  that the students try to execute back at  the mansion has  clearly failed for some reason the  sleeping agent did not have an  effect on machia at least not yet and he  was able to defeat the heroes and  continue his march towards jakku  this is really bad news for a lot of  innocent civilians  in makia's path and also for the heroes  and hero students in jakku  who already have their hands full with  the absolutely broken shigaraki  needless to say this could also be very  bad news for the heroes and hero  students who were trying to stop makia  back at the mansion  right before we saw that final page with  makia in his new form about to pummel  through a city  we also saw a couple of quick shots of  absolute  carnage near the mansion and we could  see people in hero costumes  lying motionless on the ground this was  the aftermath of the attempt by the  heroes and hero students to stop  machia the aftermath of the battle that  was happening back in chapter 280.  fat gum majestic mount lady gang orca  and other important heroes were all  there and attacking machia when the  focus of the story shifted back to jakku  and now the next thing we know all of  the heroes have been overpowered and  makia  is about to continue his journey after  leaving the heroes  and the hero students in the dust so  what happened what happened to all those  heroes  and what happened to the heroes students  did machia just kill a bunch of them  off screen did we just lose some of our  favorite boku no hero characters without  even realizing it i certainly hope not  but it's definitely possible that  makia's rampage  led to some serious casualties it's a  similar situation to what happened when  shigaraki destroyed the hospital  and an entire section of jakku city we  can't be sure yet because of all the  chaos  but it definitely seems possible that a  bunch of heroes died  this is some crazy stuff right here and  this is literally deku's worst  nightmare deku always wanted to save  everyone he wanted to protect his  friends  and innocent people what happened to  gran torino in the previous chapter is  bad enough  but now deku has to face an even more  tragic reality  izawa just lost a limb the heroes and  hero  students at the mansion might have been  killed thousands of civilians are now in  direct danger as makia plows through  multiple cities on his way to jakku  and of course shigaraki has been able to  regenerate once again  after gaining full use of his quirks at  least for the time being  obviously this turn of events isn't just  bad for deku  this is the worst case scenario for all  of japan  the last thing that anyone wanted was  makia leveling multiple cities and  killing who knows how many civilians  on his way to jakku but the reason i am  singling out deku in particular  is because he is of course the main  protagonist and he is also an extremely  emotional person who dedicated his life  to saving as many people as possible  the events of these last few chapters  are sure to fundamentally alter  deku as a person i mean just think about  it  when deku learns that some of his  friends might have been killed or  seriously injured when he learns what is  happening to civilians in all of these  different cities  and when he learns about all the pro  heroes who lost their lives  this man will never be the same again i  mean just remember how deku reacted when  one single hero  sir naidi passed away now with  potentially  thousands of people losing their lives  deku is going to blame himself for not  being able to do more  he is definitely going to take these  tragedies very personally  and i think it's safe to say that the  deku we knew from before the war arc  is now gone forever just like shigaraki  underwent a drastic character  transformation in the my villain  academia arc  deku is about to undergo a major  character transformation  as well he is about to come face to face  with  tragedy with his inability to protect  everyone  and with the dark side of the hero  society  and the pro-hero profession this is  shaping up to be  the worst case scenario this is deku's  worst nightmare  and the events of this war arc are going  to change him forever  please let me know what you guys think  did gigantomachia just kill  a bunch of heroes and hero students off  screen  or do you think that all of them were  somehow able to survive  how do you feel about shigaraki  seemingly gaining the upper hand in  battle once again  and what do you think is going to happen  next finally  how do you think deku is going to react  when he learns what just happened  at the mansion and also what is  h